# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sidechain
#
# House rule: this repo holds code, configs and prose. Every byte of data,
# every checkpoint and every paper lives OUTSIDE it, under ~/data/sidechain/
# (see CLAUDE.md). The rules below are defence in depth -- the primary
# defence is simply not putting data here.
#
# To commit something these rules would hide (a small figure, a test fixture):
#   git add -f path/to/file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- python ----
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# ---- tooling ----
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- run output ----
# cell-eval writes results.csv / agg_results.csv / *_de.csv per run. Headline
# numbers are curated into RESULTS.md; the raw output is regenerable.
runs/
cell-eval-outdir/

# ---- single-cell / ML data ----
# The formats that actually bit us: an 18 GB h5ad and a 4 GB zip sat in this
# directory before the reorg.
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
*.loom
*.mtx
*.npz
*.npy
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
vcc_data/
.lamindb/

# ---- archives & papers (these belong in ~/data/sidechain/literature/) ----
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.pdf

# ---- machine-local ----
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- internal working docs (private until first release) ----
# The repo is public and stays public -- building in the open is the point. But
# the working docs are not the product. They stay local until there is a model
# worth talking about, at which point any of them can be made public simply by
# deleting its line here and committing.
#
# Asymmetry worth remembering: publishing later is one commit; un-publishing
# later is a history rewrite plus a force-push. So the default is private.
#
# All of these were purged from git history on 2026-08-04, not merely untracked.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore has no trailing comments -- `#` only starts a comment at the
# start of a line. `plan.md  # strategy` is a pattern matching a file literally
# named "plan.md  # strategy", i.e. nothing. Keep every annotation on its own line.

# strategy, budget, timeline
plan.md
# house rules + reading budget for agent sessions
CLAUDE.md
challenges/*/CLAUDE.md
# rung ladder, prior module, eval loop
ARCHITECTURE.md
# open engineering debt
TODO.md
# completed work, moved out of TODO.md
CHANGELOG.md
# annotated paper log
literature.md
# scored runs
RESULTS.md
# subagent briefs
agents/
# term reference. Private only because its worked examples are our own results --
# strip those and it is the most publishable thing here. Good early blog post.
GLOSSARY.md

# ---- research notes ----
# Saber's hypotheses, analysis, and the future Researcher agent's findings.
# See research/README.md for the structure and how entries are added.
research/

# ---- reports ----
# Long-form explanatory write-ups: how the model works, what the data looks like,
# what we tried. Feedstock for the Sidechain blog, so they stay local until Saber
# chooses to publish a polished version.
#
# CAVEAT: untracked means NO HISTORY. A report edited three weeks from now loses
# today's version with no way back. If a report starts mattering, either move it
# into git or keep reports/ as its own repo with a private remote.
reports/
